/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A function bound inside another stores its argument into the outer function's series; one bound beside it relays to it. Cast inside a rabbit.

    A function written beside another captures the same names the same way, and takes the store over as its own. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to run-it:
    Define sink as a series of series of number.
    Bind void to tuck, given (the series of number s):
        Insert s into sink.
    Done.
    Bind void to relay, given (the series of number s):
        Cast tuck on (s).
    Done.
    Pull a rabbit.
        Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
        Cast relay on (inner).
    Done.
    State sink.
Done.
Cast run-it on ().
